      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65675,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 418,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:21:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65676,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 418,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a polyp with variably cellular stroma, a central fibrovascular core, and overlying squamous epithelium; stellate and multinucleated stromal cells, typically located at the stromal&ndash;epithelial junction and around blood vessels.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:21:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65677,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 418,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:21:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65678,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 418,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are benign but may recur locally, particularly if incompletely excised or if there is continued hormonal stimulation {10672053; 25925211; 15626915}. Complete local excision is the treatment of choice.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:21:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]